end  of zelda twilight princess  and i can see why both are shaped like a  circle have a dark grey color to them  and both were shattered into four pieces  with three of them missing  due to the similarities people in some  cases have been outright calling it the  mirror of twilight but  is that really the case is there really  a connection between the two or is it  just  a coincidental design choice well let's  take a closer look shall we  despite having solved the shrine puzzle  the stone monument itself  is never actually reassembled in game as  the pictures link took of the missing  shards were sufficient enough for  gharini to  translate the ancient writings so we  never get to see the slab in its  complete form luckily with the help of  super secret csi computer technology we  can extract the model from the game's  files  one interesting detail is that despite  the fact that all four pieces are  located quite far away from each other  at all times  they are all part of one single 3d model  which the level designers then spread  out across the map  inside the engine i didn't even have to  reassemble it myself  so is this monument supposed to be the  mirror of twilight  in my honest opinion no and there's a  couple of reasons  first we have the little fact that the  mirror was well  completely destroyed at the end of  twilight princess not split into pieces  but like totally obliterated by mitna  not exactly a  irrelevant detail i would say unless  someone built a new mirror somewhere  down the line which would make it a  replica  there is no way that the two artifacts  could be the same but even if a replica  did exist  there are far too many differences  between the two first of all there's a  clear difference in dimensions  the mirror of twilight is bigger both in  width and length while the stone slab is  thicker the decorations on the two also  differ quite a lot the monument only has  one outer ring decorated with text  and two disconnected half circles in the  center one of which has an outer bevel  while the other has an inner one  the mirror on the other hand has two  outer rims a circle in the center that  sticks out quite far  and with ornaments of a triforce symbol  two serpents among some other little  decorations around it  the back side of the mirror or the front  side depending on how you look at it  is also well a mirror a reflective  surface decorated with a complex  geometry  while the back side of the monument is  just a flat surface devoid of any  details the pedestal the mirror stands  on is also quite embellished and seems  to have been made from metals  whereas the stone tablet sits on two  stone feet so to speak  so no i do not believe the two have a  connection lore wise  could it still at least be a reference  to the mirror of twilight  sure maybe i mean anything is possible  then again  if it was then i wonder why the designs  are so radically different from one  another we can find clear references to  past games  like the crest in the castle sanctum  which is pretty much one for one to the  crests on the gates of time from skyward  sword or the three springs which are  also pretty close to the ones from  skyward sword as well  so why is the stone tablet so different  from the mirror of twilight if it was  supposed to be a reference  you would at least expect to see some of  the same decorations like maybe a faded  out triforce or the two serpents  even the file name of the 3d model  itself doesn't really say much  as it's simply called field object  search stone  very creative nintendo i think it's more  likely that the slight resemblance  between the stone tablet and the mirror  is just a coincidence there's only so  many base shapes they could have gone  with to create a monument and they  happen to have gone with a cylindrical  shape  this of course doesn't dispute a  possible connection between the zonai  and the twilight  interlopers in general i gotta be honest  i'm not entirely convinced of the  connection yet but there are definitely  some similarities that are worth  mentioning  i won't get into the twilight zone  connection here as i know of a certain  someone who is doing a very big video on  that topic very soon  and will surely be able to explain it in  way more detail than i ever could here  instead since we're here anyway let's  take a look at the one thing that does  make this piece of ancient stone masonry  special  even without being derivative of the  mirror of twilight which is of course  the mysterious writings that glow in the  dark  we've already discussed in the past that  the writings are most likely glowing  because they were made using luminous  stones which  does have a connection to the zonai of  the farren region to some degree  and some of the other structures that  make up the pomeraya ruins are  unmistakably of zonai origin  however i don't want to get too deep  into the zone eye specifically in this  video  but more so what the existence of these  writings mean because anyone who's  researched or studied anything zonai  related in breath the wild's overworld  knows that the zonai  don't seem to have had any writings none  of their prominent architecture features  anything more than stylized decorations  like swirls snake patterns and other  ornaments but never anything that looks  like an actual alphabet or even  hieroglyphics really even in the breath  while 2 trailer the only thing we can  find are cave paintings of what is  presumably ganondorf and other humanoid  beings alongside him  so how did this one single monument  suddenly feature writings which can be  translated into modern day sentences  this is not a strange question to ask  because so far the only written  languages in the zelda series we can  actually translate are hylian which  comes in a few different versions  chica writings and gerudo and in breath  of the wild these are the only written  languages we can find in the entire game  except for this one stone monument and  it gets even weirder when you think  about the implications  of this text it's supposed to serve as a  hint to open up the ancient shika shrine  but if this is  ancient zonai writing the only known  rendition of it how would they  referring to the ones who originally  carved the monument know that a shika  shrine was going to be built here  we know that the shika repurposed a  variety of different ruins to serve as a  shrine puzzle but not just those of  zonai origin but also ancient gerudo and  ancient hylian as well  so that kinda leaves us with two  different options either the zonai were  alive 10  000 years ago and were working with the  shika to create the shrine puzzle or the  shika themselves carved it into this  tablet and instead of their own language  they somehow knew the zonai alphabet and  recreated it on this monument  either way the ancient chica have some  explaining to do  as far as we know around the time that  breath the wild takes place  gorini is the only one in hyrule who  seems to understand this foreign  alphabet and is able to translate it  accordingly  unfortunately he never tells us how he  came to know the ancient texts and  decipher it whether he  and his people have any ties to this  mysterious language  or if he's just a genius at cryptography  there's already plenty of theories about  the people of laurellin and their  possible connection or even ancestry to  the zone eye so i'm gonna leave that one  up for debate for now what i would like  to know is if the text on the monument  is complete gibberish  just random symbols and nothing more or  if there's any rhyme or reason to it  i've counted the amount of characters in  the translated sentence and excluding  spaces periods and commas  it's a total of 68. on the tablet i  count approximately 64. though it's hard  to say for sure where one character  stops or starts like is this one symbol  or  two i expect that it's just random but  who knows  even if it is now maybe someday it will  be fleshed out into a real language  i'm pretty sure i'm not the first to  have made an attempt to make sense of it  but so far nobody's been able to  not that i'm aware of anyway and with a  texture as low res as this one it's  kinda hard to see the finer details of  each of the symbols  what is for sure is that whatever this  language is it is unique to any other  alphabet we've seen in the zelda series  before  it doesn't have the kanji type of  structure hylian has  or the square and blocky characteristics  of shika writings nor the elegant swirls  and curls of gerudo  rather it seems like a bit of a mishmash  there are some very angular symbols like  triangles and brackets  some curvy ones and some very simple  ones like a circle  like i said it's definitely unlike any  other alphabet found in the series  though i do want to highlight that this  is definitely not the first language  we've seen that we don't have a  translation for in twilight princess for  example we find the sky book which  contains the ancient writings of the oka  and since we oh my gosh is that a so  nice world  that was weird anyway since we only ever  get to see six characters of the oka  alphabet it's unlikely we'll ever get a  full translation of it  now i know that some of you in the  comments are already making connections  between the zonai writings and the  swirling energy in the breath while 2  trailer  and you know what i'm totally down with  that but as of right now i  don't really see it yet i'm definitely  missing some of the more angular symbols  here  as for those who are big proponents of  the twilight connection that too cannot  be ruled out  as far as we know we've never seen the  alphabet the twilight use  it could be that they simply use hylian  since they seem to speak highly into  link and ganondorf and zen too  seem to be able to understand each other  just fine but who knows maybe they did  develop their own written language  alongside it whatever the case may be  this is one mystery i definitely do hope  we can one day label as  solved thanks a lot for watching  and as always a big thanks to my  patreons and members for supporting my  channel financially  we've got tanner kossik lovelust heart  dan gamble  pedro faguera and my very own cousin  mikey joining the cause  thank you all so much and uh mikey i'll  be seeing you at the e3 live stream  it's gonna be hype that is all for now  and hopefully i will see you in the next  video  this is dawn signing off and have a good  one  [Music]  you

